WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:08.004
♪ ♪

00:00:08.005 --> 00:00:10.139
&gt;&gt; Laura: THAT IS

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.776
BOURBON STREET LIVE RIGHT NOW,

00:00:13.777 --> 00:00:14.677
FAT TUESDAY.

00:00:14.678 --> 00:00:16.646
BEGINS IN ABOUT ONE HOUR AND

00:00:16.647 --> 00:00:17.046
10 MINUTES.

00:00:17.047 --> 00:00:20.683
OUR OWN RAYMOND ARROYO,

00:00:20.684 --> 00:00:21.818
NEW ORLEANS NATIVE, INSISTED,

00:00:21.819 --> 00:00:23.152
TWISTED MY ARM THAT I GO WITH

00:00:23.153 --> 00:00:25.455
THE BIG EASY RIDE THERE AND MY

00:00:25.456 --> 00:00:26.889
FIRST MARDI GRAS PARADE.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.224
IT WAS AN ADVENTURE, AND WE

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:31.494
WANTED TO BRING YOU ALL ALONG ON

00:00:31.495 --> 00:00:32.061
THIS MARDI GRAS DAY.

00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:34.464
CHECK IT OUT.

00:00:34.465 --> 00:00:38.067
&gt;&gt; HAPPY MARDI GRAS!

00:00:38.068 --> 00:00:38.168
♪ ♪

00:00:54.184 --> 00:00:56.552
&gt;&gt; LAURA, MARDI GRAS BEGAN IN

00:00:56.553 --> 00:01:01.324
1699 HERE WHEN JOHN BAPTISTE

00:01:01.325 --> 00:01:02.859
LANDED A 60-MILE SOUTH OF

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:03.793
NEW ORLEANS, AND THEY CELEBRATED

00:01:03.794 --> 00:01:06.896
THE FIRST MARDI GRAS HERE.

00:01:06.897 --> 00:01:09.065
IT WAS ACTUALLY IN MOBILE,

00:01:09.066 --> 00:01:11.034
ALABAMA, BUT VERY QUICKLY, ONCE

00:01:11.035 --> 00:01:13.870
NEW ORLEANS WAS FOUNDED IN 1718,

00:01:13.871 --> 00:01:15.471
THIS BECAME THE EPICENTER OF

00:01:15.472 --> 00:01:18.141
MARDI GRAS.

00:01:18.142 --> 00:01:28.685
♪ ♪

00:01:28.686 --> 00:01:31.054
&gt;&gt; AS TIME WENT ON, THESE

00:01:31.055 --> 00:01:32.422
MARDI GRAS CREWS GOT BIGGER AND

00:01:32.423 --> 00:01:34.357
BIGGER, AND REMEMBER, THIS IS

00:01:34.358 --> 00:01:37.226
NOT JUST ANY FESTIVAL.

00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:41.297
THIS IS OUR PRELENT PREPARATION.

00:01:41.298 --> 00:01:42.465
&gt;&gt; Laura: DEPRIVATION.

00:01:42.466 --> 00:01:46.069
&gt;&gt; REMEMBER, THE OLD CATHOLIC

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:48.538
RIGHT, YOU COULDN'T DRINK IN THE

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:50.106
40 DAYS OF RENT, SO YOU HAD A

00:01:50.107 --> 00:01:53.843
BLOWOUT FROM JANUARY 6TH TILL

00:01:53.844 --> 00:01:54.277
ASH WEDNESDAY.

00:01:54.278 --> 00:01:56.546
THAT'S WHAT THIS IS.

00:01:56.547 --> 00:01:58.147
MARDI GRAS.

00:01:58.148 --> 00:01:58.248
♪ ♪

00:02:10.461 --> 00:02:13.496
&gt;&gt; WE HAVE TO WEAR COSTUMES,

00:02:13.497 --> 00:02:13.796
LAURA.

00:02:13.797 --> 00:02:15.598
&gt;&gt; Laura: THIS IS THE THING,

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:16.232
I'M FROM CONNECTICUT.

00:02:16.233 --> 00:02:19.635
WE HAVE A MEMORIAL DAY PARADE,

00:02:19.636 --> 00:02:21.270
GIRL SCOUTS, VETERANS.

00:02:21.271 --> 00:02:23.740
&gt;&gt; IN NEW ORLEANS, THINGS ARE

00:02:23.741 --> 00:02:24.240
LITTLE DIFFERENT.

00:02:24.241 --> 00:02:26.509
EVERYBODY WHO PARADES IN A GROUP

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:28.578
HAS TO WEAR A COSTUME, AND YOU

00:02:28.579 --> 00:02:29.245
MUST WEAR A MASK.

00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:32.181
IT IS ACTUALLY AGAINST THE LAW

00:02:32.182 --> 00:02:35.451
TO NOT MASK.

00:02:35.452 --> 00:02:35.918
A PUT THEM ON.

00:02:35.919 --> 00:02:37.320
HERE WE GO.

00:02:37.321 --> 00:02:41.891
♪ ♪

00:02:41.892 --> 00:02:44.293
&gt;&gt; ALL RIGHT, WE ARE ROLLING.

00:02:44.294 --> 00:02:44.761
&gt;&gt; LET'S DO IT.

00:02:44.762 --> 00:02:48.998
♪ ♪

00:02:48.999 --> 00:02:51.067
&gt;&gt; BEFORE YOU LOAD ON THE

00:02:51.068 --> 00:02:53.136
FLOATS, YOU HAVE TO MAKE SURE

00:02:53.137 --> 00:02:56.739
ALL OF YOUR THROWS ARE READY.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:58.108
♪ ♪

00:03:14.224 --> 00:03:14.924
&gt;&gt; Laura: THIS IS GOING TO BE

00:03:14.925 --> 00:03:16.692
REALLY FUN.

00:03:16.693 --> 00:03:20.229
&gt;&gt; THE FLOAT WE ARE WRITING IS

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.864
THE LARGEST OF MARDI GRAS, SIX

00:03:21.865 --> 00:03:22.632
SEPARATE CARS.

00:03:22.633 --> 00:03:26.869
IT IS NOT AS EASY AS IT LOOKS.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.871
&gt;&gt; Laura: ALL RIGHT, LAURA,

00:03:28.872 --> 00:03:29.539
YOUR FIRST MARDI GRAS RIDE

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.908
PAIRED WITH IT LIKE?

00:03:31.909 --> 00:03:34.644
&gt;&gt; Laura: IT'S COLD.

00:03:34.645 --> 00:03:36.078
IT'S INCREDIBLE, WE HAVE ALREADY

00:03:36.079 --> 00:03:37.814
MET GREAT FRIENDS, WE HAVE A LOT

00:03:37.815 --> 00:03:40.116
OF NEW FRIENDS ON THE FLOAT,

00:03:40.117 --> 00:03:42.318
EVERYONE IS DRINKING JUST WATER.

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:45.555
&gt;&gt; ONLY WATER.

00:03:45.556 --> 00:03:45.656
♪ ♪

00:04:11.381 --> 00:04:15.084
&gt;&gt; HAPPY MARDI GRAS!

00:04:15.085 --> 00:04:19.021
LOOK AT THIS CROWD, LAURA.

00:04:19.022 --> 00:04:20.323
UNBELIEVABLE.

00:04:20.324 --> 00:04:31.500
♪ ♪

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:33.469
&gt;&gt; WE MADE IT IN ONE PIECE.

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:36.806
I HAVE TO TELL YOU, IT'S A LONG

00:04:36.807 --> 00:04:37.073
DAY.

00:04:37.074 --> 00:04:39.642
&gt;&gt; Laura: IT'S A LONG DAY, BUT

00:04:39.643 --> 00:04:42.311
THE FACES, THE SMILES, THE

00:04:42.312 --> 00:04:43.813
PEOPLE ON THE STREET, THAT MADE

00:04:43.814 --> 00:04:44.080
IT.

00:04:44.081 --> 00:04:47.316
IT WAS FANTASTIC.

00:04:47.317 --> 00:04:49.385
EVERYBODY HAVE A HAPPY

00:04:49.386 --> 00:04:52.455
MARDI GRAS!

00:04:52.456 --> 00:04:54.423
&gt;&gt; Laura: OKAY, RAYMOND SAID

00:04:54.424 --> 00:04:56.826
WE SHOULDN'T THROW ALL OF THE

00:04:56.827 --> 00:04:57.660
GOOD DEEDS EARLY BECAUSE WE

00:04:57.661 --> 00:04:58.895
WOULD RUN OUT.

00:04:58.896 --> 00:05:00.196
WE GOT TO THE CONVENTION CENTER

00:05:00.197 --> 00:05:02.598
WHERE ALL OF THE PEOPLE ARE, WE

00:05:02.599 --> 00:05:03.766
HAD FOUR BAGS OF BEADS LEFT

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:05.635
OVER, AND WE HAD TO LEAVE THEM

00:05:05.636 --> 00:05:05.968
BEHIND.

00:05:05.969 --> 00:05:09.673
IT WAS SO MUCH FUN.

